WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:20.967
Riley spent the first few minutes at the gym stretching—and feeling sorry for herself.

2
00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:30.971
"It's not fair that Jordan gets all the attention and money," she thought. "Meanwhile I get stuck with Jordan's hand-me-downs!"

3
00:00:30.972 --> 00:00:37.137
But as Riley's body slowly warmed up, she could feel her mind calm down.

4
00:00:37.138 --> 00:00:46.203
Jordan's accident had been a nightmare for the whole family. Poor Jordan had pain all the time, and she couldn't ride . . .

5
00:00:46.204 --> 00:00:52.614
Riley suddenly felt embarrassed. She'd probably sounded like a spoiled brat to her father.

6
00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:59.860
She knew she'd have to apologize, even though a small, bitter lump still sat in her stomach.

7
00:00:59.861 --> 00:01:05.271
Riley glanced at the clock, deciding to test her ankle on a stationary bike.

8
00:01:05.272 --> 00:01:10.514
As she headed toward the bike room, she glanced into a small workout room.

9
00:01:10.515 --> 00:01:23.837
"That's Quinn," Riley thought. "What's she doing?" She watched Quinn run forward and throw herself onto a floor mat.

10
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:33.410
"Is she practicing a fall?" Riley wondered. She watched Quinn do it again.

11
00:01:33.411 --> 00:01:40.060
"She's falling all wrong," Riley muttered. "She's going to get hurt."

12
00:01:40.061 --> 00:01:45.415
Riley pushed open the door. "Hey, Quinn."

13
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:54.647
"Oh, hi. What do you want?" Quinn didn't sound mean. She just looked puzzled by Riley's sudden appearance.

14
00:01:54.648 --> 00:01:58.303
"I saw you practicing a fall."

15
00:01:58.304 --> 00:02:00.921
Quinn nodded, her face brightening.

16
00:02:00.922 --> 00:02:06.144
"I saw a video online that showed how to fall off a bike safely, and I've been practicing at home.

17
00:02:06.145 --> 00:02:11.634
But I had to stop when I broke a lamp in the living room. My mom told me to practice here."

18
00:02:11.635 --> 00:02:18.888
Riley laughed. "I smashed a couple of photo frames at my house learning to fall."

19
00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:25.626
"Watch this!" Quinn crouched, and then sprang up and ran down the mat.

20
00:02:25.627 --> 00:02:34.699
She took a small leap, stretched out her hands, and did a strange handspring-like roll.

21
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.469
"What do you think?" Quinn asked.

22
00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:46.757
"Um . . ." Riley hesitated. "I don't know who made that video, but you probably shouldn't fall like that."

23
00:02:46.758 --> 00:02:50.859
Quinn put her hands on her hips. "Why not?"

24
00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.946
Riley tried to remember how Jordan had explained it to her.

25
00:02:54.947 --> 00:03:01.266
Jordan was a great teacher, one who could correct Riley's mistakes without making her feel silly.

26
00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:06.271
"When you're falling, your instinct is to throw out your hands as you go down.

27
00:03:06.272 --> 00:03:09.919
But you should never put out your hands to break your fall."

28
00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.324
"That doesn't make sense." Quinn frowned.

29
00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:22.819
"I know it sounds weird," Riley said. "But if you reach out like that, your hands will take the weight of your falling body."

30
00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:29.318
Riley dropped onto her knees and threw out her hands to show Quinn what she was talking about.

31
00:03:29.319 --> 00:03:35.460
"The force of hitting the ground moves up your arm until it finds a weak spot, and breaks it.

32
00:03:35.461 --> 00:03:38.637
Most of the time that weak spot is your wrist.

33
00:03:38.638 --> 00:03:44.477
It could also be your elbow or even your collarbone. So don't use your hands."

34
00:03:44.478 --> 00:03:46.886
"Then what am I supposed to use?"

35
00:03:46.887 --> 00:03:52.629
"You're supposed to tuck your arms into your body. Then you can roll with the fall."

36
00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:59.636
Riley put her arms to her sides and fell onto the mat, rolling forward.

37
00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:06.375
"This way the force of your fall is distributed around your whole body. You're less likely to get hurt."

38
00:04:06.376 --> 00:04:11.792
Quinn scowled. "That's not what the guy says on the video. He says—"

39
00:04:11.793 --> 00:04:20.127
"He's giving out bad advice," Riley interrupted. "My sister is a great rider, and she taught me that fall."

40
00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:26.784
"Yeah, I've heard all about Miss Know-it-All Jordan," Quinn said, rolling her eyes.

41
00:04:26.785 --> 00:04:31.599
"I'm surprised you take advice from someone who crashed and can't even ride anymore."

42
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.163
Riley's cheeks flamed. "Don't talk about my sister that way!

43
00:04:36.163 --> 00:04:41.014
She knows more about riding than some stupid guy on some stupid online video."

44
00:04:41.015 --> 00:04:52.001
"Thanks for your . . . uh, help," Quinn said sarcastically. "I'm out of here." She grabbed her workout bag and glared at Riley.

45
00:04:52.002 --> 00:04:58.588
"You're pretending to be nice, but I can tell what you're really doing—trying to sabotage me for the tryout!"

46
00:04:58.589 --> 00:05:05.904
Quinn marched out of the room, slamming the door so hard the glass rattled.

47
00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:13.731
"Sabotage her?" Riley muttered. "I was just trying to help."

48
00:05:13.732 --> 00:05:22.383
The rest of the week passed quickly. Riley apologized to her father and tried to push the unpleasant scene with Quinn out of her mind.

49
00:05:22.384 --> 00:05:29.049
Quinn definitely got under Riley's skin, but the tryout was tomorrow, and Riley had to focus.

50
00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:35.801
That night after dinner Riley wheeled her bike out of the garage and began her pre-race prep.

51
00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:42.284
She started at the top of the bike, checking the shifters to make sure they were tight.

52
00:05:42.285 --> 00:05:45.631
Then she checked the brakes and the brake pads.

53
00:05:45.632 --> 00:05:56.872
She made sure the seat height was right and tightened the bolts so the seat wouldn't wiggle. Next she oiled the chain.

54
00:05:56.873 --> 00:06:05.286
Jordan had shown Riley how to replace the foam grips on the handlebars with tape a few weeks back, and now the tape was starting to fray.

55
00:06:05.287 --> 00:06:11.763
Riley pulled new tape out of her tool kit, and then stood there, trying to remember how to wrap it.

56
00:06:11.764 --> 00:06:16.930
"Need some help?" Jordan asked from the doorway, leaning on her crutches.

57
00:06:16.931 --> 00:06:23.670
Riley held out the tape. "Yeah, I can't remember how you did this."

58
00:06:23.671 --> 00:06:25.583
"I'll see what I can do."

59
00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:33.912
Riley grabbed a folding chair from a shelf in the garage, and Jordan sat on it with a sigh.

60
00:06:33.913 --> 00:06:43.826
"I can't wait to get off these crutches," she murmured, unwrapping the old tape from Riley's bike. "Maybe next month."

61
00:06:43.827 --> 00:06:52.741
Riley watched her sister remove the old tape and expertly wind new tape around the handlebars.

62
00:06:52.742 --> 00:06:59.486
"Tape is so much better than those foam grips," Jordan said. "It looks cooler too."

63
00:06:59.487 --> 00:07:02.637
"Much cooler," Riley agreed.

64
00:07:02.638 --> 00:07:06.966
"What's next?" Jordan looked the bike over with an expert eye.

65
00:07:06.967 --> 00:07:12.973
"Tire pressure and the treads? Have you tested the brakes? How's your helmet? Any cracks?"

66
00:07:12.974 --> 00:07:22.964
Riley smiled. She used to get annoyed when Jordan checked up on her like this. Now, before the tryout, it felt reassuring.

67
00:07:22.965 --> 00:07:29.042
"All good," Riley said. "I'm going to do a quick ride through the neighborhood.

68
00:07:29.043 --> 00:07:37.535
Tell Mom I'll be back soon." She strapped on her helmet and flew down the street.

69
00:07:37.536 --> 00:07:44.360
Riley tested the bike's gears and brakes as she rode the familiar streets.

70
00:07:44.361 --> 00:07:48.683
She turned onto a long street and leaned down, picking up speed.

71
00:07:48.684 --> 00:07:55.190
She felt a twinge in her ankle, but nothing serious. Confident, she put more weight on it.

72
00:07:55.191 --> 00:08:07.496
"It feels fine," Riley thought happily. She hoped her ankle—and the rest of her—felt this strong tomorrow.
